{"title":"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A box contains chips, each of which is red, white, or blue. The number of blue chips is at least half the number of white chips, and at most one third the number of red chips. The number which are white or blue is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79030abeb688469b5ffc2e1c4e37fee225a529e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The minimum number of red chips is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/2/8822bc6c7498f194ab8be6ffb83d837fdbff500c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }24\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }33\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }45\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }54\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }57$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the number of white be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. The number of blue is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/643e1765342cf3807fd7d130ee679b71ecd4789b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. So we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397a1a1a56a4a6383b80ccdc9f32bac266f83e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+x-y=55\\rightarrow 3x-y=55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"247\" height=\"16\" />. We take mod 3 to find y. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/f/75f04bb959603307bb8a9208565b2771a12325bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55=1\\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, so blue is 1 more than half white. The number of whites is then 36, and the number of blues is 19. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/7827fdd41e97be21a76a0efab587a3149104d078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19*3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }57}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"134\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p><br />\n~yofro\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME\" title=\"1971 AHSME\">1971 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1971 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1971\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"c